# External dogfood (PLAN.md decision 41): restful-booker (https://restful-booker.herokuapp.com) is
# a public QA-practice API we don't control — a more honest acceptance target than our own
# automationTestPOC sample app. Credentials here are the API's own publicly-documented test
# account (not a real secret), still routed through env(...)/.env like any other credential so the
# redaction path gets dogfooded too.
#
# ============================================================================================
# **THE ONLY HOST IN THIS REPO WE DO NOT OWN. FUNCTIONAL API TESTS ONLY.** (ruling 2026-08-18)
#
#   - **No load or performance runs.** This is somebody else's free sandbox. Every other perf rung
#     in this repo points at apiV2 on `:4001`, which we start and can saturate as we like.
#   - **No security or vulnerability scans.** Pointing a pentest tool at a host we do not own is
#     not ours to authorise, whatever a config says. Note what is deliberately absent below: there
#     is **no `authorized target` line**, and that is the mechanism rather than an oversight —
#     tflw refuses every scan and every probe against an unaffirmed origin (`TF060`, D21 layer 2).
#     Adding one is the single edit that would change this, so do not.
#   - **Not on CI, and not on any schedule.** A suite that runs on every push is traffic we send to
#     a stranger's server forever. Run it by hand, when you have a reason to:
#
#         cd tflw-acceptance/restful-booker && npx tflw run --no-color
#
# All three are asserted by `npm run verify:external-targets`, which also fails if a *new* external
# target appears anywhere in this repo without somebody writing down what it is for. They were all
# true before that guard existed — true by omission, which is not the same as true.
# ============================================================================================

env booker default
  api "https://restful-booker.herokuapp.com"

session admin
  api POST /auth body { username: env(BOOKER_USER), password: env(BOOKER_PASS) }
  expect status equals 200
  capture body.token as token
  header "Cookie" is "token={token}"

require env BOOKER_USER, BOOKER_PASS
